      {
        "title": "Summary of Gaps by Priority",
        "content": "| Priority | Gap | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| **High** | `toErrorResponse()` (errors.ts) | Entire error contract; PG error code branches completely untested |\n| **High** | `Conn` class + hub functions | Core realtime infrastructure; pure in-memory, zero external deps |\n| **High** | `rateLimit()` | Token bucket math; replenishment edge cases |\n| **High** | `conversations.ts` route | Race condition handler uses bypass `db` — only path where `db` is used for user input |\n| **Medium** | `notify()` self-filter | Silent filtering bug would cause actors to see their own notifications |\n| **Medium** | `guardExecute()` negative take, defaults | Backward pagination correctness |\n| **Medium** | `uploads.ts` BLOCKED regex + `orgVisible` validation | Security: XSS via SVG if regex has gaps |\n| **Medium** | `rtc.ts` HMAC credential | TURN secret never verified in test |\n| **Medium** | `org.ts` lifecycle hooks | `createDefaultGroup` idempotency, `removeFromOrganization` cascade |\n| **Low** | `calls.ts` `sanitizeMedia()` | Easy to extract and unit test |\n| **Low** | Missing policy scenarios (message reactions, event RSVP cross-org, type immutability) | ZenStack `@deny('update', true)` never exercised |\n\nThe highest-value additions would be **errors.test.ts** (pure unit, no DB needed), **hub.test.ts** (pure unit, no DB needed), and **conversations.test.ts** (integration, covers the only route with a bypass-`db` code path).",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
